{#-
Macros for the template, imported with
``{% from 'macros.jinja' import ... %}``. Copier resolves imports from the
repository root (not from ``_subdirectory``), so this file is never rendered
into a project. Macros instead of Jinja extensions: extensions are an unsafe
Copier feature and would make every user pass ``--trust``.
-#}

{#- Escape ``value`` for use between double quotes: valid inside a TOML basic
string ("...") and a Python string literal ("..." or """..."""), as long as
``value`` has no control characters (prompt answers are single lines). -#}
{%- macro escape_double_quoted(value) -%}
{{ value | string | replace('\\', '\\\\') | replace('"', '\\"') }}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Render ``value`` as a Python string literal, quotes included, with the
quotes ``ruff format`` would pick: double quotes, unless the value has more
double than single quotes. A generated project then passes
``ruff format --check`` whatever the prompt answer was. -#}
{%- macro python_string(value) -%}
{%- set text = value | string | replace('\\', '\\\\') -%}
{%- if text.count('"') > text.count("'") -%}
'{{ text | replace("'", "\\'") }}'
{%- else -%}
"{{ text | replace('"', '\\"') }}"
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Licenses that only ask for the copyright notice to accompany copies of
the work, which the LICENSE file already does: per-file notices add nothing,
so the generated Ruff config ignores CPY001 and the ``.py`` files get no
header. Every other license gets both. -#}
{%- set licenses_without_file_notices = [
    'MIT license', 'BSD license', 'ISC license'
] -%}

{#- The comment block that starts every generated ``.py`` file when the
license calls for per-file notices (see above), empty otherwise. It matches
Ruff's CPY001 pattern, adds an SPDX identifier for the open source licenses,
and ends with ``trailer`` (a blank line by default) to separate it from the
code. The name loses surrounding whitespace (W291) and trailing backslashes,
which make Ruff take the comment for commented-out code (ERA001). -#}
{%- macro copyright_header(open_source_license, full_name, trailer='\n') -%}
{%- if open_source_license not in licenses_without_file_notices -%}
{%- set name = full_name | string | trim
    | regex_replace('[\\s\\\\]+\\Z', '') -%}
{{ '# Copyright (c) ' ~ ('%Y' | strftime) ~ (', ' ~ name if name else '') ~ '\n' }}
{%- if open_source_license == 'Apache Software License 2.0' -%}
{{ '# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n' }}
{%- elif open_source_license == 'GNU General Public License v3' -%}
{{ '# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later\n' }}
{%- endif -%}
{{ trailer }}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endmacro -%}
